and Asia. It operates through Platform and Products segments. The company offers connected machines, accessories, and materials for users to create personalized birthday cards, mugs, T-shirts, and large-scale interior decorations. Its connected machines, which are used to cut, write, score, and create decorative effects on paper, adhesive vinyl, iron-on vinyl, wood, and leather, comprise Cricut Joy family, Cricut Explore family, Cricut Maker family, and Cricut Venture. The company also provides Cricut Design Space, a cloud-based software that integrates with connected machines to enable users to create and work on projects across desktop and mobile devices; Cricut Access and Cricut Access Premium subscription offerings; and in-app purchases of images, fonts, and projects. In addition, it offers a range of accessories and materials, such as Cricut EasyPress, Cricut Mug Press, hand tools, machine replacement tools and blades, and project materials, such as vinyl and iron-on. Further, the company provides craft, DIY, home d\u00e9cor products, and extensions. It offers its products through its third-party brick-and-mortar and online retail partners; and its website cricut.com, as well as through a network of distributors. Cricut, Inc. was formerly known as Provo Craft & Novelty, Inc. and changed its name to Cricut, Inc. in March 2018. The company was incorporated in 1969 and is headquartered in South Jordan, Utah.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ashish  Arora | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $8.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 700 people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, declining at 14%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Stock-based compensation of $50K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Cricut, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.8B market cap on $709M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -7% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 16-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 45%.","Accruals are elevated at -21.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 12.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 133% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3289119928017887},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Cricut (NASDAQ:CRCT) Releases Quarterly Earnings Results, Beats Estimates By $0.08 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/cricut-nasdaqcrct-releases-quarterly-earnings-results-beats-estimates-by-0-08-eps.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793895179.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(CRCT) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/34/CRCT_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_110526064001_1793878801.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793878801.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cricut (CRCT) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/cricut-crct-q3-2026-earnings-154459000.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793807517.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Cricut: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/cricut-3-key-takeaways-long-004702053.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793839622.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":1,"scope":"company","ta